    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.clue\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nnvim has a default binding for z\\<CR>, which moves the current line to the top of the screen.  When mini.clue is in use, it eats the \\<CR>, and one has to type z\\<CR>\\<CR> to get the desired behavior.  I'm not sure if there are any other bindings that include a \\<CR>, but if so, they would presumably have the same issue.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.10.2\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. install mini.clue with suggested config that has trigger for 'z'\r\n3. type z\\<CR>\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nShould move current line to top of screen.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nEnters the 'z' prefix without the typed \\<CR>",
