        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI am afraid there is no clear solution to this:\r\n- 'mini.clue' *needs* some key to execute the currently typed keys because there can be a mapping for it. I would not recommend having this kind of setup (like have both `<Leader>s` and `<Leader>st` mappings, for example), but some cases it might be justified. And not being able to execute some mappings is worth than having an inconvenience during some other mappings (which I'd argue are not common).\r\n- To be perfectly honest, I was surprised to learn about `z<CR>` because I always use `zt` for that. It has better mnemonic (`z` - \"top\"), is easier to type, and I'd argue more ergonomic (preserves cursor column instead of moving to the first non-blank character). If you want to preserve `z<CR>` behavior, I'd recommend remapping `zt` with something like `nnoremap zt zt^`.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
