            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Sorry to revive this, but I'm having the same issue (using neovim-orgmode, where `<Leader><CR>` maps to a context-aware \"continue in the next line with the current type of paragraph\" type of action (`org-meta-cr`).\n\nAs far as I can tell (and according to mini-clue), that is the only mapping involving CR, and the behavior is the same as @rothskeller described. What exactly does mini-clue need here? All other mappings work find without doubling any input (and I really need clue to get the hang of all those mappings, so: thank you!). If there is some internal mapping-to-a-dummy-key going on, why not use something not found on most keyboards, like F24?",
