        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> What exactly does mini-clue need here? All other mappings work find without doubling any input (and I really need clue to get the hang of all those mappings, so: thank you!). If there is some internal mapping-to-a-dummy-key going on, why not use something not found on most keyboards, like F24?\n\nThe `<CR>` is a part of ['mini.clue' lifecycle](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-clue.html#miniclue-key-query-process-lifecycle), same as other special keys: `<Esc>`, `<C-c>`, `<BS>`, `<C-u>`, `<C-d>`. They have special meaning when advancing the key query process that 'mini.clue' provides and nothing to do with \"mapping-to-a-dummy-key\".\n\nSo I am afraid the suggestion here is to either not use triggers that result into mapping with these special keys or prefer other keys. Whichever keys are chosen for these special actions, there will always be a possibility of this sort of collisions. The current choice makes the most sense in what keys are intended to do.",
