            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Wow, that was quick! Thank you, and sorry for not looking at the docs first. That section explains everything really well! The examples given starting with `g` also explain why that behavior can't be easily deactivated even though all my _personal_ mappings only distinct sequences.\n\nWhat I can gather from [what I think is the corresponding source location](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.clue/blob/d846600d4664dc793aa29859ad135b1fd25d648b/lua/mini/clue.lua#L1396), this behavior is hardcoded. I guess I need to get creative, hitting three keys just for a smarter linebreak is a bit much.",
