        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> What I can gather from [what I think is the corresponding source location](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.clue/blob/d846600d4664dc793aa29859ad135b1fd25d648b/lua/mini/clue.lua#L1396), this behavior is hardcoded. I guess I need to get creative, hitting three keys just for a smarter linebreak is a bit much.\n\nYes, all non-scroll special keys are hardcoded because they both are the first choices for their respective functionalities and making them configurable won't solve the problem of needing such keys per se.",
